id: pm-gh1456
title: "GH-1456: Discoverable SDK-backed bulk creation with JSONL and keyed upsert"
description: "Extend the shipped atomic SDK/CLI mutation primitive with a discoverable bulk-create workflow, JSONL input and optional keyed upsert. The existing pm item mutate surface already commits ordered create/update/close batches and must be reused rather than reimplemented."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",bulk-mutations,github-intake
created_at: "2026-10-13T18:12:30.417Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T19:01:37.296Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-15T15:10:34.121Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-15T15:10:34.121Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Document and execute the existing atomic create batch as the immediate recovery; Any create-many adapter delegates to public SDK transaction primitives; JSONL/ref resolution and keyed upsert preserve input order and validate before persistence; Interrupted or repeated imports preserve complete history and stable idempotency
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "pm item mutate accepts JSON Lines, single records and op-less create documents (pm create field names, optionally {ref,item}), reads them with --from <path>, synthesizes row-<n> aliases, returns an input-ordered rows receipt, derives a stable transaction id from the document bytes when --transaction-id is omitted, and resolves --upsert-key against existing items via the new SDK planner planItemMutationDocument (schema hydrated through the transaction preview's guarded loader under the dry-run configuration-only scope). pm_mutate accepts item rows, upsertKey and an optional transactionId. pm create many refuses with bulk_create_route. Journal/plan mismatch is the typed transaction_plan_mismatch refusal."
expected_result: "Agents create an ordered batch through the existing SDK-backed atomic CLI surface, with discoverable JSONL/ref input and stable keyed-upsert semantics that retain history and idempotency."
actual_result: "Sandbox and integration tests: 2-record JSON Lines import committed in one transaction, replay of the same file returned recovered:true with no duplicates, upsert by a declared custom field updated the matched item and created the unmatched one, dry-run under the configuration-only scope validated with declared fields present, missing/duplicate/ambiguous keys refused before any write, MCP document rows with @ref forward references and upsertKey committed. Linked tests pass; exact coverage 100/100/100/100."
